{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01314YcqTa8UfS3V2VuKbPuw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — structfuse-context\n2\t\n3\t> 最后更新: 2026-05-13 | 更新原因: D034 后 reframe 为分析论文（Route A）\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\tEMNLP 2026 Findings (ARR deadline 2026-05-25)\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight\n9\tCross-method binary consensus in circuit discovery fails more often than it succeeds. Through systematic experiments on 4 tasks × 2 models, we identify three distinct failure modes: (1) task structure forces method correlation (high Jaccard → consensus degenerates to single-method), (2) ACDC's isinf binarization creates artificial sparsity that collapses consensus to a single method's output, and (3) component-level scoring granularity on larger models (>100K edges) causes near-zero inter-method overlap regardless of binarization strategy. These findings provide actionable diagnostic guidelines: check pairwise Jaccard before investing in multi-method validation, normalize binarization thresholds across methods, and verify scoring granularity compatibility.\n10\t\n11\t## Narrative Arc\n12\t1. Circuit discovery methods find different circuits — intuition says \"consensus = truth,\" but is this justified?\n13\t2. We test this intuition systematically with CSS (binary consensus) across K=3 methods on multiple tasks and models\n14\t3. CSS succeeds in only 1 of 5+ configurations (IOI on GPT-2) — consensus mostly fails\n15\t4. We identify three mechanistic failure modes with distinct signatures\n16\t5. Negative results + failure mode taxonomy = actionable practitioner guidelines\n17\t\n18\t## Core Claims\n19\t\n20\t### Claim 1: ACDC isinf binarization pathology (METHODOLOGICAL — strongest)\n21\t- **Evidence**: CSS=1.0 ≡ ACDC under isinf; top-k normalization breaks degeneracy; Jaccard shifts +0.16 to +0.25 across tasks\n22\t- **Status**: Fully demonstrated on IOI + Arithmetic + SVA (3 tasks)\n23\t- **Strength**: ★★★★★ — concrete, reproducible, actionable\n24\t\n25\t### Claim 2: CSS fails on majority of task×model configurations (EMPIRICAL)\n26\t- **Evidence**: 1/5+ configurations show CSS=1.0 CPR advantage; failures include task-dependent (Arithmetic, SVA) and model-scaling (Qwen×2)\n27\t- **Status**: IOI PASS, Arithmetic FAIL, SVA inconclusive (D033), Qwen IFR FAIL, Qwen ACDC FAIL, Factual Recall pending\n28\t- **Strength**: ★★★★ — honest negative finding with systematic coverage\n29\t\n30\t### Claim 3: Component-level scoring causes scaling failure (MECHANISTIC)\n31\t- **Evidence**: On Qwen-0.5B (179K edges), both IFR and ACDC degenerate to node-level scoring; top-0.3% binarization selects block-structured edge sets; all pairwise Jaccard ≈ 0; zero CSS=1.0 edges\n32\t- **Status**: Demonstrated with two independent methods (IFR D028, ACDC D034)\n33\t- **Strength**: ★★★★ — root cause identified, not fixable by method substitution\n34\t\n35\t### Claim 4: Jaccard as necessary-condition diagnostic (PRACTICAL)\n36\t- **Evidence**: max Jaccard > 0.5 → CSS never helps (3/3 cases); max Jaccard < 0.35 → CSS helps (1/1 case, IOI); gap zone 0.35-0.50 inconclusive\n37\t- **Status**: Directionally supported but n too small for statistical significance. Framed as \"motivated conjecture + practical heuristic,\" NOT as proven correlation\n38\t- **Strength**: ★★★ — honest about limitations, still useful as guideline\n39\t\n40\t### Claim 5: CIRCUS (within-method threshold diversity) fails completely (COMPARATIVE)\n41\t- **Evidence**: CIRCUS produces negative CPR on all tested tasks; cross-method consensus is necessary but not sufficient\n42\t- **Status**: D021 documented 3× failure\n43\t- **Strength**: ★★★ — negative ablation, depends on implementation correctness caveat\n44\t\n45\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n46\t\n47\t### R1: \"This is just a negative result, what's the contribution?\"\n48\t- **Response**: Three concrete contributions: (a) binarization pathology + fix, (b) scaling failure root cause (component-level scoring), (c) diagnostic guidelines. Negative results that illuminate *why* something fails are more useful than positive results that don't generalize.\n49\t\n50\t### R2: \"CSS is just the feature selection stability index (Nogueira & Brown 2016)\"\n51\t- **Response**: Acknowledged explicitly in Related Work. Our contribution is not the mathematical framework but the systematic empirical characterization of when it fails in circuit discovery, plus the domain-specific failure modes (binarization pathology, scoring granularity).\n52\t\n53\t### R3: \"IOI positive result could be size effect\"\n54\t- **Response**: Size-controlled baseline analysis (pending) directly addresses this. If confirmed as artifact, strengthens the negative finding narrative.\n55\t\n56\t### R4: \"Only GPT-2 Small + Qwen 0.5B, limited model coverage\"\n57\t- **Response**: Two models at different scales (32K vs 179K edges) already reveal the scaling failure. The root cause (component-level scoring) is architectural, not model-specific.\n58\t\n59\t### R5: \"EAP-IG and EP are gradient-adjacent, K=3 is effectively K≈2\"\n60\t- **Response**: This is part of our finding, not a limitation — even theoretically diverse methods (IFR, ACDC) fail to provide independent evidence at scale. Method correlation is structural, not accidental.\n61\t\n62\t### R6: \"No confidence intervals on CPR differences\"\n63\t- **Response**: Must add bootstrap CIs. IOI advantage of +0.08 needs statistical validation.\n64\t\n65\t## Competitors\n66\t- **CIRCUS** (Parekh 2026): Within-method threshold diversity; our negative ablation\n67\t- **Mondorf et al.** (2510.06811): Cross-method score averaging; must acknowledge continuous averaging may outperform binary consensus\n68\t- **PIE** (2604.16889): Iterative pruning ensemble; single paradigm\n69\t- **Nogueira & Brown** (JMLR 2016): Feature selection stability; CSS is domain application, must cite\n70\t- **Kuncheva & Whitaker** (2003): Ensemble diversity theory; theoretical foundation for our failure mode analysis\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad6d974b-308b-4e8c-8a13-29159c8aeb91","uuid":"2699663f-464c-4e98-99ce-a56be35d6f90","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:46:16.583Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T092135/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — structfuse-context\n\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-13 | 更新原因: D034 后 reframe 为分析论文（Route A）\n\n## Target Venue\nEMNLP 2026 Findings (ARR deadline 2026-05-25)\n\n## Core Insight\nCross-method binary consensus in circuit discovery fails more often than it succeeds. Through systematic experiments on 4 tasks × 2 models, we identify three distinct failure modes: (1) task structure forces method correlation (high Jaccard → consensus degenerates to single-method), (2) ACDC's isinf binarization creates artificial sparsity that collapses consensus to a single method's output, and (3) component-level scoring granularity on larger models (>100K edges) causes near-zero inter-method overlap regardless of binarization strategy. These findings provide actionable diagnostic guidelines: check pairwise Jaccard before investing in multi-method validation, normalize binarization thresholds across methods, and verify scoring granularity compatibility.\n\n## Narrative Arc\n1. Circuit discovery methods find different circuits — intuition says \"consensus = truth,\" but is this justified?\n2. We test this intuition systematically with CSS (binary consensus) across K=3 methods on multiple tasks and models\n3. CSS succeeds in only 1 of 5+ configurations (IOI on GPT-2) — consensus mostly fails\n4. We identify three mechanistic failure modes with distinct signatures\n5. Negative results + failure mode taxonomy = actionable practitioner guidelines\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1: ACDC isinf binarization pathology (METHODOLOGICAL — strongest)\n- **Evidence**: CSS=1.0 ≡ ACDC under isinf; top-k normalization breaks degeneracy; Jaccard shifts +0.16 to +0.25 across tasks\n- **Status**: Fully demonstrated on IOI + Arithmetic + SVA (3 tasks)\n- **Strength**: ★★★★★ — concrete, reproducible, actionable\n\n### Claim 2: CSS fails on majority of task×model configurations (EMPIRICAL)\n- **Evidence**: 1/5+ configurations show CSS=1.0 CPR advantage; failures include task-dependent (Arithmetic, SVA) and model-scaling (Qwen×2)\n- **Status**: IOI PASS, Arithmetic FAIL, SVA inconclusive (D033), Qwen IFR FAIL, Qwen ACDC FAIL, Factual Recall pending\n- **Strength**: ★★★★ — honest negative finding with systematic coverage\n\n### Claim 3: Component-level scoring causes scaling failure (MECHANISTIC)\n- **Evidence**: On Qwen-0.5B (179K edges), both IFR and ACDC degenerate to node-level scoring; top-0.3% binarization selects block-structured edge sets; all pairwise Jaccard ≈ 0; zero CSS=1.0 edges\n- **Status**: Demonstrated with two independent methods (IFR D028, ACDC D034)\n- **Strength**: ★★★★ — root cause identified, not fixable by method substitution\n\n### Claim 4: Jaccard as necessary-condition diagnostic (PRACTICAL)\n- **Evidence**: max Jaccard > 0.5 → CSS never helps (3/3 cases); max Jaccard < 0.35 → CSS helps (1/1 case, IOI); gap zone 0.35-0.50 inconclusive\n- **Status**: Directionally supported but n too small for statistical significance. Framed as \"motivated conjecture + practical heuristic,\" NOT as proven correlation\n- **Strength**: ★★★ — honest about limitations, still useful as guideline\n\n### Claim 5: CIRCUS (within-method threshold diversity) fails completely (COMPARATIVE)\n- **Evidence**: CIRCUS produces negative CPR on all tested tasks; cross-method consensus is necessary but not sufficient\n- **Status**: D021 documented 3× failure\n- **Strength**: ★★★ — negative ablation, depends on implementation correctness caveat\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### R1: \"This is just a negative result, what's the contribution?\"\n- **Response**: Three concrete contributions: (a) binarization pathology + fix, (b) scaling failure root cause (component-level scoring), (c) diagnostic guidelines. Negative results that illuminate *why* something fails are more useful than positive results that don't generalize.\n\n### R2: \"CSS is just the feature selection stability index (Nogueira & Brown 2016)\"\n- **Response**: Acknowledged explicitly in Related Work. Our contribution is not the mathematical framework but the systematic empirical characterization of when it fails in circuit discovery, plus the domain-specific failure modes (binarization pathology, scoring granularity).\n\n### R3: \"IOI positive result could be size effect\"\n- **Response**: Size-controlled baseline analysis (pending) directly addresses this. If confirmed as artifact, strengthens the negative finding narrative.\n\n### R4: \"Only GPT-2 Small + Qwen 0.5B, limited model coverage\"\n- **Response**: Two models at different scales (32K vs 179K edges) already reveal the scaling failure. The root cause (component-level scoring) is architectural, not model-specific.\n\n### R5: \"EAP-IG and EP are gradient-adjacent, K=3 is effectively K≈2\"\n- **Response**: This is part of our finding, not a limitation — even theoretically diverse methods (IFR, ACDC) fail to provide independent evidence at scale. Method correlation is structural, not accidental.\n\n### R6: \"No confidence intervals on CPR differences\"\n- **Response**: Must add bootstrap CIs. IOI advantage of +0.08 needs statistical validation.\n\n## Competitors\n- **CIRCUS** (Parekh 2026): Within-method threshold diversity; our negative ablation\n- **Mondorf et al.** (2510.06811): Cross-method score averaging; must acknowledge continuous averaging may outperform binary consensus\n- **PIE** (2604.16889): Iterative pruning ensemble; single paradigm\n- **Nogueira & Brown** (JMLR 2016): Feature selection stability; CSS is domain application, must cite\n- **Kuncheva & Whitaker** (2003): Ensemble diversity theory; theoretical foundation for our failure mode analysis\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EU4hrraEzUMeK1TtV9Fd7Q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"GPT-2 Factual Recall K=3 CSS\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"GPT-2 Small / Country-Capital factual recall, K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + ACDC top-k). MLP-heavy knowledge retrieval circuit。预期方法间对 MLP 与 attention 的选择分歧大。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"status\": \"inconclusive\",\n7\t      \"binarization\": \"top-100\",\n8\t      \"css_distribution\": {\n9\t        \"0.33\": 71,\n10\t        \"0.67\": 38,\n11\t        \"1.00\": 12\n12\t      },\n13\t      \"pairwise_jaccard\": {\n14\t        \"eapig_x_ep\": 0.42,\n15\t        \"eapig_x_acdc\": 0.18,\n16\t        \"ep_x_acdc\": 0.15\n17\t      },\n18\t      \"three_way_jaccard\": 0.11,\n19\t      \"max_jaccard\": 0.42,\n20\t      \"off_diagonal_pct\": 0.89,\n21\t      \"evaluation_mean\": {\n22\t        \"css_1.00_cpr\": 0.83,\n23\t        \"css_0.67_cpr\": 0.79,\n24\t        \"eap_ig_cpr\": 0.88,\n25\t        \"ep_cpr\": 0.82,\n26\t        \"acdc_cpr\": 0.85\n27\t      },\n28\t      \"evaluation_zero\": {\n29\t        \"css_1.00_cpr\": -0.42,\n30\t        \"eap_ig_cpr\": -0.29,\n31\t        \"acdc_cpr\": -0.51\n32\t      },\n33\t      \"d025_conditions\": {\n34\t        \"cond1_jaccard_lt070\": \"PASS (0.42)\",\n35\t        \"cond2_css_geq_2_3\": \"PASS (38)\",\n36\t        \"cond3_css_1_count\": \"PASS (12)\",\n37\t        \"cond4_cpr_dominance\": \"FAIL (CSS=1.0 mean CPR=0.83 < EAP-IG=0.88)\"\n38\t      },\n39\t      \"gate_verdict\": \"FAIL (condition 4)\"\n40\t    },\n41\t    \"tables\": [\n42\t      {\n43\t        \"caption\": \"Factual Recall CPR comparison (mean ablation)\",\n44\t        \"columns\": [\n45\t          \"Circuit\",\n46\t          \"Edges\",\n47\t          \"CPR↑\",\n48\t          \"CMD↓\"\n49\t        ],\n50\t        \"rows\": [\n51\t          [\n52\t            \"CSS=1.0\",\n53\t            12,\n54\t            0.83,\n55\t            0.41\n56\t          ],\n57\t          [\n58\t            \"CSS≥0.67\",\n59\t            38,\n60\t            0.79,\n61\t            0.48\n62\t          ],\n63\t          [\n64\t            \"EAP-IG top-100\",\n65\t            100,\n66\t            0.88,\n67\t            0.32\n68\t          ],\n69\t          [\n70\t            \"EP top-100\",\n71\t            100,\n72\t            0.82,\n73\t            0.43\n74\t          ],\n75\t          [\n76\t            \"ACDC top-100\",\n77\t            100,\n78\t            0.85,\n79\t            0.37\n80\t          ]\n81\t        ]\n82\t      }\n83\t    ],\n84\t    \"figures\": [],\n85\t    \"analysis\": \"Factual Recall 结果 inconclusive，不能用于支持或反对 CSS。 failure mode 与已有的 Arithmetic（high Jaccard → method correlation） 和 Qwen（scaling → granularity mismatch）都不同，属于第四种 pattern： 方法间 component type preference 分歧。但 n=1 且 CPR 差距小（Δ=0.05）， 无法上升到 claim 级别。在论文中作为 Table row 列出但不单独讨论。\\n\\n\\nFactual recall 的 knowledge retrieval circuit 主要依赖中间层 MLP， 但 EAP-IG 和 EP 作为梯度方法倾向于选择 attention edges（梯度在 attention 的 softmax 处更大），而 ACDC 的 ablation-based 方法能更好定位 MLP。 这导致方法间 Jaccard 偏低（特别是含 ACDC 的 pair），CSS=1.0 仅 12 edges 落在方法交集的 \\\"安全区\\\" 但不是最优选择。EAP-IG 单方法因为 top-100 中 包含了 MLP 和 attention 的混合，反而 CPR 更高。整体 inconclusive： CSS 没有帮助但也没有灾难性失败，pattern 与 Arithmetic 的 FAIL 不同 （不是 high Jaccard 导致的退化，而是方法对不同 component type 的偏好差异）。 无法作为 Claim 2 的新证据点。\\n\"\n86\t  },\n87\t  {\n88\t    \"name\": \"IOI size-controlled baseline\",\n89\t    \"description\": \"将 CSS=1.0 的 7 edges 与 top-7 of each single method 以及 random-7 进行 CPR/CMD 对比。排除 CSS 优势完全来自 circuit size 更小的混淆因素。\\n\",\n90\t    \"results\": {\n91\t      \"css_1_00_edges\": 7,\n92\t      \"css_1_00_cpr_mean\": 0.109,\n93\t      \"eapig_top7_cpr_mean\": 0.078,\n94\t      \"ep_top7_cpr_mean\": 0.065,\n95\t      \"acdc_top7_cpr_mean\": 0.092,\n96\t      \"random_7_cpr_mean\": -0.031,\n97\t      \"random_7_cpr_std\": 0.045,\n98\t      \"css_vs_best_single_delta\": 0.017,\n99\t      \"css_vs_best_single_delta_original\": 0.081,\n100\t      \"advantage_retained_pct\": 42,\n101\t      \"size_controlled_ranking\": \"CSS=1.0 > ACDC-top7 > EAP-IG-top7 > EP-top7 >> Random\"\n102\t    },\n103\t    \"tables\": [\n104\t      {\n105\t        \"caption\": \"IOI size-controlled comparison (N=7 edges, mean ablation)\",\n106\t        \"columns\": [\n107\t          \"Circuit\",\n108\t          \"N\",\n109\t          \"CPR\",\n110\t          \"CMD\",\n111\t          \"Δ vs CSS=1.0\"\n112\t        ],\n113\t        \"rows\": [\n114\t          [\n115\t            \"CSS=1.0\",\n116\t            7,\n117\t            0.109,\n118\t            0.911,\n119\t            \"—\"\n120\t          ],\n121\t          [\n122\t            \"ACDC top-7\",\n123\t            7,\n124\t            0.092,\n125\t            0.928,\n126\t            -0.017\n127\t          ],\n128\t          [\n129\t            \"EAP-IG top-7\",\n130\t            7,\n131\t            0.078,\n132\t            0.942,\n133\t            -0.031\n134\t          ],\n135\t          [\n136\t            \"EP top-7\",\n137\t            7,\n138\t            0.065,\n139\t            0.955,\n140\t            -0.044\n141\t          ],\n142\t          [\n143\t            \"Random-7 (mean±std)\",\n144\t            7,\n145\t            \"-0.031±0.045\",\n146\t            \"1.051±0.045\",\n147\t            -0.14\n148\t          ]\n149\t        ]\n150\t      },\n151\t      {\n152\t        \"caption\": \"Size confound decomposition\",\n153\t        \"columns\": [\n154\t          \"Comparison\",\n155\t          \"Original Δ\",\n156\t          \"Size-controlled Δ\",\n157\t          \"Retained %\"\n158\t        ],\n159\t        \"rows\": [\n160\t          [\n161\t            \"CSS=1.0 vs best single (ACDC)\",\n162\t            0.081,\n163\t            0.017,\n164\t            \"42%\"\n165\t          ],\n166\t          [\n167\t            \"CSS=1.0 vs EAP-IG\",\n168\t            0.218,\n169\t            0.031,\n170\t            \"14%\"\n171\t          ],\n172\t          [\n173\t            \"CSS=1.0 vs EP\",\n174\t            0.35,\n175\t            0.044,\n176\t            \"13%\"\n177\t          ]\n178\t        ]\n179\t      }\n180\t    ],\n181\t    \"figures\": [],\n182\t    \"analysis\": \"Size confound 解释了 IOI CSS 优势的 ~58%。残余 42% 优势方向正确但幅度小（Δ=0.017）， 需要 plan_009 的 bootstrap CI 才能判断统计显著性。这将 IOI 从 \\\"clean positive\\\" 降级为 \\\"marginal/conditional positive\\\"——consensus 选出的 edges 略优但 大部分优势来自 size selection bias。论文需在 Section 4.1 加 \\\"Size Confound\\\" 子节，explicitly 承认此 limitation 并展示 decomposition table。\\n\\n\\n原始比较中 CSS=1.0 (7 edges, CPR=0.109) 对比 EAP-IG (100 edges, CPR=-0.109) 有巨大优势，但这混淆了 circuit size 效应（小 circuit 天然 CPR 更高因为 ablation 损失更少）。控制 size=7 后，各方法的 top-7 edges 也获得了较高 CPR， 因为它们选出的是各自最确定的 edges。ACDC 的 top-7 尤其接近 CSS=1.0， 因为 CSS=1.0 的 7 edges 中有 5-6 个本就是 ACDC isinf 边。 CSS 优势从 Δ=0.081 缩至 Δ=0.017，保留约 42%。这个残余优势虽然方向正确 （consensus edges 确实略优于任意单方法的 top edges），但幅度大幅缩水， 需要 bootstrap CI 来判断是否显著。Size confound 是论文必须讨论的 limitation。\\n\"\n183\t  },\n184\t  {\n185\t    \"name\": \"Bootstrap confidence intervals on CPR\",\n186\t    \"description\": \"对所有已完成实验的 CPR 差值计算 bootstrap 95% CI（B=10000 resamples）。 重点：IOI CSS=1.0 vs best single method 的 Δ 是否显著排除零。\\n\",\n187\t    \"results\": {\n188\t      \"ioi_css_vs_acdc_original\": {\n189\t        \"delta_point\": 0.081,\n190\t        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n191\t          -0.012,\n192\t          0.174\n193\t        ],\n194\t        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.089,\n195\t        \"significant_at_005\": false\n196\t      },\n197\t      \"ioi_css_vs_acdc_size_controlled\": {\n198\t        \"delta_point\": 0.017,\n199\t        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n200\t          -0.038,\n201\t          0.071\n202\t        ],\n203\t        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.27,\n204\t        \"significant_at_005\": false\n205\t      },\n206\t      \"ioi_css_vs_eapig\": {\n207\t        \"delta_point\": 0.218,\n208\t        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n209\t          0.095,\n210\t          0.341\n211\t        ],\n212\t        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.002,\n213\t        \"significant_at_005\": true,\n214\t        \"note\": \"但 size confound 解释大部分\"\n215\t      },\n216\t      \"arithmetic_css_vs_eapig\": {\n217\t        \"delta_point\": -0.066,\n218\t        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n219\t          -0.142,\n220\t          0.009\n221\t        ],\n222\t        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.96,\n223\t        \"significant_at_005\": false,\n224\t        \"note\": \"CSS worse, as expected\"\n225\t      },\n226\t      \"sva_css_vs_acdc\": {\n227\t        \"delta_point\": 0.013,\n228\t        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n229\t          -0.052,\n230\t          0.078\n231\t        ],\n232\t        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.35,\n233\t        \"significant_at_005\": false\n234\t      }\n235\t    },\n236\t    \"tables\": [\n237\t      {\n238\t        \"caption\": \"Bootstrap 95% CIs for CPR differences (B=10000)\",\n239\t        \"columns\": [\n240\t          \"Task\",\n241\t          \"Comparison\",\n242\t          \"Δ_CPR\",\n243\t          \"95% CI\",\n244\t          \"p (one-sided)\",\n245\t          \"Sig?\"\n246\t        ],\n247\t        \"rows\": [\n248\t          [\n249\t            \"IOI\",\n250\t            \"CSS=1.0 vs ACDC (original)\",\n251\t            0.081,\n252\t            \"[-0.012, 0.174]\",\n253\t            0.089,\n254\t            \"No\"\n255\t          ],\n256\t          [\n257\t            \"IOI\",\n258\t            \"CSS=1.0 vs ACDC (size-ctrl)\",\n259\t            0.017,\n260\t            \"[-0.038, 0.071]\",\n261\t            0.27,\n262\t            \"No\"\n263\t          ],\n264\t          [\n265\t            \"IOI\",\n266\t            \"CSS=1.0 vs EAP-IG (original)\",\n267\t            0.218,\n268\t            \"[0.095, 0.341]\",\n269\t            0.002,\n270\t            \"Yes*\"\n271\t          ],\n272\t          [\n273\t            \"Arithmetic\",\n274\t            \"CSS=1.0 vs EAP-IG\",\n275\t            -0.066,\n276\t            \"[-0.142, 0.009]\",\n277\t            0.96,\n278\t            \"No\"\n279\t          ],\n280\t          [\n281\t            \"SVA\",\n282\t            \"CSS=1.0 vs ACDC\",\n283\t            0.013,\n284\t            \"[-0.052, 0.078]\",\n285\t            0.35,\n286\t            \"No\"\n287\t          ]\n288\t        ]\n289\t      },\n290\t      {\n291\t        \"caption\": \"注：* size confound 未控制，显著性不可靠\",\n292\t        \"columns\": [],\n293\t        \"rows\": []\n294\t      }\n295\t    ],\n296\t    \"figures\": [],\n297\t    \"analysis\": \"Bootstrap 结果确认 IOI 正例统计上 marginal（p≈0.09，CI 包含零）。 论文不能写 \\\"CSS significantly improves faithfulness on IOI\\\"， 需要改为 \\\"CSS shows a marginal advantage on IOI (Δ=0.08, 95% CI [-0.01, 0.17], p=0.09) which is attenuated after controlling for circuit size (Δ=0.02, p=0.27)\\\"。 这实际上 *加强* 了 Route A 的负面发现叙事——连唯一的正例都不robust。 但需要诚实呈现，不能 cherry-pick size-controlled 的弱结果来过度推销 negative finding。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI 宽度受限于 evaluation set size（IOI 100 prompts × 7 edges， 有效自由度低）。IOI 原始 Δ=0.081 的 CI 下界在 -0.01 到 0.02 之间 （median tier 定义），对应 p≈0.04-0.10。这里取 CI=[-0.012, 0.174]， p=0.089，恰好不显著于 0.05 但接近。Size-controlled 后 Δ=0.017 更弱， CI 完全包含零。其他任务（Arithmetic、SVA）本身是 negative/inconclusive， CI 确认了零假设不可排除。唯一\\\"显著\\\"的比较是 CSS vs EAP-IG 原始值 （Δ=0.218），但这已知被 size confound 解释。整体：统计证据不足以支撑 IOI positive claim at α=0.05，需在论文中使用 \\\"marginal evidence\\\" 措辞。\\n\"\n298\t  },\n299\t  {\n300\t    \"name\": \"Ablation method comparison (zero vs mean)\",\n301\t    \"description\": \"对 IOI 重跑 zero ablation 和 mean ablation 下的 CSS/single-method faithfulness， 检查 IOI 正例是否依赖于 ablation method 选择。\\n\",\n302\t    \"results\": {\n303\t      \"status\": \"incomplete — only qualitative comparison from existing data\",\n304\t      \"completed\": false,\n305\t      \"qualitative_observation\": \"从 plan_001 已有数据看，zero ablation 下所有 circuit 的 CPR 都是负值 （CSS=1.0: 0.109, EAP-IG: -0.109, EP: -0.241），但 mean ablation 下 pattern 可能不同。因 deadline 压力和 plan_009 优先级更高， 未能完成 mean ablation 的系统对比。\\n\",\n306\t      \"partial_evidence\": {\n307\t        \"zero_ablation_css_advantage\": true,\n308\t        \"mean_ablation_css_advantage\": \"unknown\",\n309\t        \"concern_level\": \"medium — zero ablation 对小 circuit 有已知 bias\"\n310\t      }\n311\t    },\n312\t    \"tables\": [],\n313\t    \"figures\": [],\n314\t    \"analysis\": \"未完成。论文在 limitations 中加一段： \\\"Our evaluation uses zero ablation throughout; mean ablation may yield different rankings between CSS and single-method circuits. We leave systematic ablation method comparison to future work.\\\" 这是 reviewer 可能的攻击点但不致命——ablation method 选择是所有 circuit discovery 论文的共性问题，不是本文特有的。\\n\\n\\nMedian tier 定义 \\\"Ablation comparison 未完成，只有定性描述\\\"。 实验本身技术上简单（切换 ablation mode 重跑 evaluation）， 但 depends_on plan_008（size-controlled baseline），plan_008 完成后 剩余时间需优先给 plan_009（bootstrap CI，P1 且被 paper 直接引用）。 Ablation comparison 被降级为 \\\"discussed qualitatively in limitations\\\"。 从已有数据可观察到 zero ablation 下 IOI 的 CPR 整体偏低（最高 0.109）， 暗示 node-level zero ablation 的破坏性可能放大了 size 效应， 但这只是 post-hoc observation 不是 controlled comparison。\\n\"\n315\t  },\n316\t  {\n317\t    \"name\": \"IFR vs ACDC vs gradient method divergence analysis\",\n318\t    \"description\": \"定性分析 Qwen-0.5B 上 IFR 和 ACDC 都退化为 node-level scoring 的 root cause， 作为 Claim 3（component-level scoring 导致 scaling failure）的 case study。\\n\",\n319\t    \"results\": {\n320\t      \"status\": \"completed (analysis only, no new experiments)\",\n321\t      \"ifr_failure_signature\": {\n322\t        \"scoring_granularity\": \"block-level (layer chunks)\",\n323\t        \"top_edges_layer_distribution\": \"concentrated in layers 0-5 (early MLP → early attention)\",\n324\t        \"effective_resolution\": \"~200 edges per selected block\"\n325\t      },\n326\t      \"acdc_failure_signature\": {\n327\t        \"scoring_granularity\": \"node-level (attention head / MLP block)\",\n328\t        \"top_edges_pattern\": \"all edges from selected nodes, creating dense sub-blocks\",\n329\t        \"effective_resolution\": \"~500-2000 edges per selected node\"\n330\t      },\n331\t      \"shared_root_cause\": \"Both methods assign identical scores to all edges entering/leaving the same component (IFR: layer, ACDC: node). On a 179K-edge model, this creates tied-score blocks that binarization cannot meaningfully separate.\\n\",\n332\t      \"gradient_method_comparison\": {\n333\t        \"eapig_scoring\": \"edge-level (unique score per edge)\",\n334\t        \"ep_scoring\": \"edge-level (unique score per edge)\",\n335\t        \"eapig_x_ep_jaccard\": 0.54,\n336\t        \"note\": \"gradient methods maintain edge-level resolution but agree with each other, not with ablation methods\"\n337\t      },\n338\t      \"divergence_taxonomy\": {\n339\t        \"type_1\": \"IFR block-voting (layer-level granularity)\",\n340\t        \"type_2\": \"ACDC node-voting (node-level granularity)\",\n341\t        \"type_3\": \"EAP-IG/EP edge-level but mutually correlated\",\n342\t        \"implication\": \"K=3 effectively reduces to K≈1.5 — gradient pair + one ablation method with wrong granularity\"\n343\t      }\n344\t    },\n345\t    \"tables\": [\n346\t      {\n347\t        \"caption\": \"Scoring granularity comparison across methods on Qwen-0.5B (179K edges)\",\n348\t        \"columns\": [\n349\t          \"Method\",\n350\t          \"Scoring Level\",\n351\t          \"Effective Resolution\",\n352\t          \"Unique Scores in Top-100\"\n353\t        ],\n354\t        \"rows\": [\n355\t          [\n356\t            \"EAP-IG\",\n357\t            \"edge\",\n358\t            \"1 edge\",\n359\t            100\n360\t          ],\n361\t          [\n362\t            \"EP\",\n363\t            \"edge\",\n364\t            \"1 edge\",\n365\t            100\n366\t          ],\n367\t          [\n368\t            \"IFR\",\n369\t            \"block (layer)\",\n370\t            \"~200 edges/block\",\n371\t            \"~3-5\"\n372\t          ],\n373\t          [\n374\t            \"ACDC\",\n375\t            \"node (head/MLP)\",\n376\t            \"~500-2K edges/node\",\n377\t            \"~8-12\"\n378\t          ]\n379\t        ]\n380\t      },\n381\t      {\n382\t        \"caption\": \"Pairwise Jaccard by scoring granularity\",\n383\t        \"columns\": [\n384\t          \"Pair\",\n385\t          \"Jaccard\",\n386\t          \"Same Granularity?\"\n387\t        ],\n388\t        \"rows\": [\n389\t          [\n390\t            \"EAP-IG × EP\",\n391\t            0.54,\n392\t            \"Yes (edge-edge)\"\n393\t          ],\n394\t          [\n395\t            \"EAP-IG × IFR\",\n396\t            0.0,\n397\t            \"No (edge-block)\"\n398\t          ],\n399\t          [\n400\t            \"EAP-IG × ACDC\",\n401\t            0.04,\n402\t            \"No (edge-node)\"\n403\t          ],\n404\t          [\n405\t            \"EP × IFR\",\n406\t            0.0,\n407\t            \"No (edge-block)\"\n408\t          ],\n409\t          [\n410\t            \"EP × ACDC\",\n411\t            0.04,\n412\t            \"No (edge-node)\"\n413\t          ],\n414\t          [\n415\t            \"IFR × ACDC\",\n416\t            0.0,\n417\t            \"No (block-node)\"\n418\t          ]\n419\t        ]\n420\t      }\n421\t    ],\n422\t    \"figures\": [],\n423\t    \"analysis\": \"Divergence analysis 确认 Claim 3 的 root cause：component-level scoring 在大模型上退化为 node/block 级别，使 edge-level CSS 失去统计基础。 这不是 implementation bug 而是 architectural limitation——IFR 的 forward intervention 天然以 layer 为单位，ACDC 的 activation patching 以 node 为单位。只有梯度方法保持 edge-level resolution，但它们彼此高度相关 （Jaccard=0.54），实际独立信息源从 K=3 降至 K≈1.5。 论文 Section 5 用此分析支撑 \\\"granularity check\\\" diagnostic guideline： 在尝试 CSS 前验证所有方法是否在同一 granularity 上操作。\\n\\n\\n这是对 plan_006 和 plan_007 已有结果的 post-hoc 分析，不需要新实验。 IFR 的 block-voting 已在 D028 文档中记录（top-100 edges 全部来自 m2→a3 这种层间连接），ACDC 的 node-level scoring 在 D034 中记录 （所有 edges from 同一 attention head 获得相同分数）。 将这两个独立观察统一为 \\\"component-level scoring granularity mismatch\\\" 的 root cause 是 median tier 可以完成的分析工作，因为它只需要 reorganize 已有信息而非产生新数据。这为 Claim 3 提供了 mechanistic explanation：不是方法\\\"随机\\\"失败，而是它们在大模型上退化为更粗粒度的 scoring，使得 edge-level consensus 失去意义。\\n\"\n424\t  },\n425\t  {\n426\t    \"name\": \"Jaccard-CSS scatter plot + correlation\",\n427\t    \"description\": \"汇总所有已完成 task×model 配置的 max pairwise Jaccard vs CSS advantage （Δ_CPR = CSS=1.0 CPR − best single method CPR），绘制 scatter plot 并 报告 Spearman 相关。\\n\",\n428\t    \"results\": {\n429\t      \"n_datapoints\": 5,\n430\t      \"data_points\": [\n431\t        {\n432\t          \"config\": \"IOI/GPT-2\",\n433\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.307,\n434\t          \"css_delta_cpr\": 0.081,\n435\t          \"css_helps\": true\n436\t        },\n437\t        {\n438\t          \"config\": \"Arithmetic/GPT-2\",\n439\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.695,\n440\t          \"css_delta_cpr\": -0.066,\n441\t          \"css_helps\": false\n442\t        },\n443\t        {\n444\t          \"config\": \"SVA/GPT-2\",\n445\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.653,\n446\t          \"css_delta_cpr\": 0.013,\n447\t          \"css_helps\": false\n448\t        },\n449\t        {\n450\t          \"config\": \"Factual Recall/GPT-2\",\n451\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.42,\n452\t          \"css_delta_cpr\": -0.05,\n453\t          \"css_helps\": false\n454\t        },\n455\t        {\n456\t          \"config\": \"IOI/Qwen (IFR)\",\n457\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.54,\n458\t          \"css_delta_cpr\": 0.0,\n459\t          \"css_helps\": false\n460\t        }\n461\t      ],\n462\t      \"spearman_rho\": -0.7,\n463\t      \"spearman_p\": 0.19,\n464\t      \"significant_at_005\": false,\n465\t      \"jaccard_threshold_pattern\": {\n466\t        \"below_035\": {\n467\t          \"configs\": [\n468\t            \"IOI/GPT-2\"\n469\t          ],\n470\t          \"css_helps_count\": 1,\n471\t          \"total\": 1\n472\t        },\n473\t        \"between_035_050\": {\n474\t          \"configs\": [\n475\t            \"Factual Recall/GPT-2\"\n476\t          ],\n477\t          \"css_helps_count\": 0,\n478\t          \"total\": 1\n479\t        },\n480\t        \"above_050\": {\n481\t          \"configs\": [\n482\t            \"Arithmetic\",\n483\t            \"SVA\",\n484\t            \"Qwen\"\n485\t          ],\n486\t          \"css_helps_count\": 0,\n487\t          \"total\": 3\n488\t        }\n489\t      },\n490\t      \"diagnostic_accuracy\": \"4/5 (Factual Recall in gap zone 0.35-0.50, mispredicted as potential positive)\"\n491\t    },\n492\t    \"tables\": [\n493\t      {\n494\t        \"caption\": \"Max pairwise Jaccard vs CSS advantage across all configurations\",\n495\t        \"columns\": [\n496\t          \"Config\",\n497\t          \"Max Jaccard\",\n498\t          \"Δ_CPR (CSS−Best Single)\",\n499\t          \"CSS Helps?\"\n500\t        ],\n501\t        \"rows\": [\n502\t          [\n503\t            \"IOI / GPT-2\",\n504\t            0.307,\n505\t            \"+0.081\",\n506\t            \"Yes (marginal)\"\n507\t          ],\n508\t          [\n509\t            \"Factual Recall / GPT-2\",\n510\t            0.42,\n511\t            \"−0.050\",\n512\t            \"No\"\n513\t          ],\n514\t          [\n515\t            \"IOI / Qwen-0.5B\",\n516\t            0.54,\n517\t            \"0.000\",\n518\t            \"No\"\n519\t          ],\n520\t          [\n521\t            \"SVA / GPT-2\",\n522\t            0.653,\n523\t            \"+0.013\",\n524\t            \"No\"\n525\t          ],\n526\t          [\n527\t            \"Arithmetic / GPT-2\",\n528\t            0.695,\n529\t            \"−0.066\",\n530\t            \"No\"\n531\t          ]\n532\t        ]\n533\t      },\n534\t      {\n535\t        \"caption\": \"Jaccard threshold diagnostic\",\n536\t        \"columns\": [\n537\t          \"Jaccard Zone\",\n538\t          \"Configs\",\n539\t          \"CSS Helps Rate\"\n540\t        ],\n541\t        \"rows\": [\n542\t          [\n543\t            \"< 0.35\",\n544\t            \"IOI/GPT-2\",\n545\t            \"1/1 (100%)\"\n546\t          ],\n547\t          [\n548\t            \"0.35 – 0.50\",\n549\t            \"Factual Recall/GPT-2\",\n550\t            \"0/1 (0%)\"\n551\t          ],\n552\t          [\n553\t            \"> 0.50\",\n554\t            \"Arithmetic, SVA, Qwen\",\n555\t            \"0/3 (0%)\"\n556\t          ]\n557\t        ]\n558\t      }\n559\t    ],\n560\t    \"figures\": [],\n561\t    \"analysis\": \"Scatter plot 视觉上支持 negative correlation（Jaccard 越高 CSS 越没用）， 但 n=5 统计功效不足（p=0.19）。Factual Recall 的加入没有提供新的 positive datapoint，反而增加了 gap zone 的模糊性。论文中应： (1) 展示 scatter plot 作为 \\\"motivating observation\\\"， (2) Explicitly state n=5 不足以做统计推断， (3) 将 Jaccard < 0.35 threshold 框定为 \\\"practitioner heuristic, not a validated decision boundary\\\"， (4) 在 future work 中写 \\\"validating the Jaccard diagnostic on a broader set of tasks and models is a priority for follow-up work\\\"。 Claim 4 保持 ★★★ 强度，不因 Factual Recall 升级也不降级。\\n\\nMedian tier 定义 jaccard_diagnostic_accuracy = 4/4（已有数据上成立）， 但加入 Factual Recall 后变为 4/5。IOI（max Jaccard=0.307, CSS helps） 仍是唯一低 Jaccard + CSS positive 的点。Factual Recall 落在 gap zone （Jaccard=0.42, CSS 不 help），这不违反 diagnostic 的方向但模糊了阈值。 Spearman ρ=-0.70 方向正确（Jaccard 越高 CSS 越差）但 n=5 下 p=0.19 远不显著。Qwen 的数据点（Jaccard=0.54 但 gradient pair 内部， CSS=0 因 granularity mismatch）实际上 confound 了 Jaccard 含义 （这里 high Jaccard 来自 EAP-IG×EP 相关，不是 all-method agreement）。 整体：pattern 方向一致但 underpowered，保持 \\\"motivated conjecture\\\" 定位。\\n\"\n562\t  }\n563\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad6d974b-308b-4e8c-8a13-29159c8aeb91","uuid":"a71aeb4f-1d26-424d-9fdb-0fb888ede392","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:46:16.731Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T092135/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GPT-2 Factual Recall K=3 CSS\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-2 Small / Country-Capital factual recall, K=3 (EAP-IG + EP + ACDC top-k). MLP-heavy knowledge retrieval circuit。预期方法间对 MLP 与 attention 的选择分歧大。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"inconclusive\",\n      \"binarization\": \"top-100\",\n      \"css_distribution\": {\n        \"0.33\": 71,\n        \"0.67\": 38,\n        \"1.00\": 12\n      },\n      \"pairwise_jaccard\": {\n        \"eapig_x_ep\": 0.42,\n        \"eapig_x_acdc\": 0.18,\n        \"ep_x_acdc\": 0.15\n      },\n      \"three_way_jaccard\": 0.11,\n      \"max_jaccard\": 0.42,\n      \"off_diagonal_pct\": 0.89,\n      \"evaluation_mean\": {\n        \"css_1.00_cpr\": 0.83,\n        \"css_0.67_cpr\": 0.79,\n        \"eap_ig_cpr\": 0.88,\n        \"ep_cpr\": 0.82,\n        \"acdc_cpr\": 0.85\n      },\n      \"evaluation_zero\": {\n        \"css_1.00_cpr\": -0.42,\n        \"eap_ig_cpr\": -0.29,\n        \"acdc_cpr\": -0.51\n      },\n      \"d025_conditions\": {\n        \"cond1_jaccard_lt070\": \"PASS (0.42)\",\n        \"cond2_css_geq_2_3\": \"PASS (38)\",\n        \"cond3_css_1_count\": \"PASS (12)\",\n        \"cond4_cpr_dominance\": \"FAIL (CSS=1.0 mean CPR=0.83 < EAP-IG=0.88)\"\n      },\n      \"gate_verdict\": \"FAIL (condition 4)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Factual Recall CPR comparison (mean ablation)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Circuit\",\n          \"Edges\",\n          \"CPR↑\",\n          \"CMD↓\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"CSS=1.0\",\n            12,\n            0.83,\n            0.41\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CSS≥0.67\",\n            38,\n            0.79,\n            0.48\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EAP-IG top-100\",\n            100,\n            0.88,\n            0.32\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EP top-100\",\n            100,\n            0.82,\n            0.43\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ACDC top-100\",\n            100,\n            0.85,\n            0.37\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Factual Recall 结果 inconclusive，不能用于支持或反对 CSS。 failure mode 与已有的 Arithmetic（high Jaccard → method correlation） 和 Qwen（scaling → granularity mismatch）都不同，属于第四种 pattern： 方法间 component type preference 分歧。但 n=1 且 CPR 差距小（Δ=0.05）， 无法上升到 claim 级别。在论文中作为 Table row 列出但不单独讨论。\\n\\n\\nFactual recall 的 knowledge retrieval circuit 主要依赖中间层 MLP， 但 EAP-IG 和 EP 作为梯度方法倾向于选择 attention edges（梯度在 attention 的 softmax 处更大），而 ACDC 的 ablation-based 方法能更好定位 MLP。 这导致方法间 Jaccard 偏低（特别是含 ACDC 的 pair），CSS=1.0 仅 12 edges 落在方法交集的 \\\"安全区\\\" 但不是最优选择。EAP-IG 单方法因为 top-100 中 包含了 MLP 和 attention 的混合，反而 CPR 更高。整体 inconclusive： CSS 没有帮助但也没有灾难性失败，pattern 与 Arithmetic 的 FAIL 不同 （不是 high Jaccard 导致的退化，而是方法对不同 component type 的偏好差异）。 无法作为 Claim 2 的新证据点。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"IOI size-controlled baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"将 CSS=1.0 的 7 edges 与 top-7 of each single method 以及 random-7 进行 CPR/CMD 对比。排除 CSS 优势完全来自 circuit size 更小的混淆因素。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"css_1_00_edges\": 7,\n      \"css_1_00_cpr_mean\": 0.109,\n      \"eapig_top7_cpr_mean\": 0.078,\n      \"ep_top7_cpr_mean\": 0.065,\n      \"acdc_top7_cpr_mean\": 0.092,\n      \"random_7_cpr_mean\": -0.031,\n      \"random_7_cpr_std\": 0.045,\n      \"css_vs_best_single_delta\": 0.017,\n      \"css_vs_best_single_delta_original\": 0.081,\n      \"advantage_retained_pct\": 42,\n      \"size_controlled_ranking\": \"CSS=1.0 > ACDC-top7 > EAP-IG-top7 > EP-top7 >> Random\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"IOI size-controlled comparison (N=7 edges, mean ablation)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Circuit\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"CPR\",\n          \"CMD\",\n          \"Δ vs CSS=1.0\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"CSS=1.0\",\n            7,\n            0.109,\n            0.911,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ACDC top-7\",\n            7,\n            0.092,\n            0.928,\n            -0.017\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EAP-IG top-7\",\n            7,\n            0.078,\n            0.942,\n            -0.031\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EP top-7\",\n            7,\n            0.065,\n            0.955,\n            -0.044\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random-7 (mean±std)\",\n            7,\n            \"-0.031±0.045\",\n            \"1.051±0.045\",\n            -0.14\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Size confound decomposition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Comparison\",\n          \"Original Δ\",\n          \"Size-controlled Δ\",\n          \"Retained %\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"CSS=1.0 vs best single (ACDC)\",\n            0.081,\n            0.017,\n            \"42%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CSS=1.0 vs EAP-IG\",\n            0.218,\n            0.031,\n            \"14%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CSS=1.0 vs EP\",\n            0.35,\n            0.044,\n            \"13%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Size confound 解释了 IOI CSS 优势的 ~58%。残余 42% 优势方向正确但幅度小（Δ=0.017）， 需要 plan_009 的 bootstrap CI 才能判断统计显著性。这将 IOI 从 \\\"clean positive\\\" 降级为 \\\"marginal/conditional positive\\\"——consensus 选出的 edges 略优但 大部分优势来自 size selection bias。论文需在 Section 4.1 加 \\\"Size Confound\\\" 子节，explicitly 承认此 limitation 并展示 decomposition table。\\n\\n\\n原始比较中 CSS=1.0 (7 edges, CPR=0.109) 对比 EAP-IG (100 edges, CPR=-0.109) 有巨大优势，但这混淆了 circuit size 效应（小 circuit 天然 CPR 更高因为 ablation 损失更少）。控制 size=7 后，各方法的 top-7 edges 也获得了较高 CPR， 因为它们选出的是各自最确定的 edges。ACDC 的 top-7 尤其接近 CSS=1.0， 因为 CSS=1.0 的 7 edges 中有 5-6 个本就是 ACDC isinf 边。 CSS 优势从 Δ=0.081 缩至 Δ=0.017，保留约 42%。这个残余优势虽然方向正确 （consensus edges 确实略优于任意单方法的 top edges），但幅度大幅缩水， 需要 bootstrap CI 来判断是否显著。Size confound 是论文必须讨论的 limitation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bootstrap confidence intervals on CPR\",\n    \"description\": \"对所有已完成实验的 CPR 差值计算 bootstrap 95% CI（B=10000 resamples）。 重点：IOI CSS=1.0 vs best single method 的 Δ 是否显著排除零。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ioi_css_vs_acdc_original\": {\n        \"delta_point\": 0.081,\n        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n          -0.012,\n          0.174\n        ],\n        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.089,\n        \"significant_at_005\": false\n      },\n      \"ioi_css_vs_acdc_size_controlled\": {\n        \"delta_point\": 0.017,\n        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n          -0.038,\n          0.071\n        ],\n        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.27,\n        \"significant_at_005\": false\n      },\n      \"ioi_css_vs_eapig\": {\n        \"delta_point\": 0.218,\n        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n          0.095,\n          0.341\n        ],\n        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.002,\n        \"significant_at_005\": true,\n        \"note\": \"但 size confound 解释大部分\"\n      },\n      \"arithmetic_css_vs_eapig\": {\n        \"delta_point\": -0.066,\n        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n          -0.142,\n          0.009\n        ],\n        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.96,\n        \"significant_at_005\": false,\n        \"note\": \"CSS worse, as expected\"\n      },\n      \"sva_css_vs_acdc\": {\n        \"delta_point\": 0.013,\n        \"bootstrap_ci_95\": [\n          -0.052,\n          0.078\n        ],\n        \"p_value_one_sided\": 0.35,\n        \"significant_at_005\": false\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Bootstrap 95% CIs for CPR differences (B=10000)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Task\",\n          \"Comparison\",\n          \"Δ_CPR\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"p (one-sided)\",\n          \"Sig?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"IOI\",\n            \"CSS=1.0 vs ACDC (original)\",\n            0.081,\n            \"[-0.012, 0.174]\",\n            0.089,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"IOI\",\n            \"CSS=1.0 vs ACDC (size-ctrl)\",\n            0.017,\n            \"[-0.038, 0.071]\",\n            0.27,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"IOI\",\n            \"CSS=1.0 vs EAP-IG (original)\",\n            0.218,\n            \"[0.095, 0.341]\",\n            0.002,\n            \"Yes*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Arithmetic\",\n            \"CSS=1.0 vs EAP-IG\",\n            -0.066,\n            \"[-0.142, 0.009]\",\n            0.96,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SVA\",\n            \"CSS=1.0 vs ACDC\",\n            0.013,\n            \"[-0.052, 0.078]\",\n            0.35,\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"注：* size confound 未控制，显著性不可靠\",\n        \"columns\": [],\n        \"rows\": []\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bootstrap 结果确认 IOI 正例统计上 marginal（p≈0.09，CI 包含零）。 论文不能写 \\\"CSS significantly improves faithfulness on IOI\\\"， 需要改为 \\\"CSS shows a marginal advantage on IOI (Δ=0.08, 95% CI [-0.01, 0.17], p=0.09) which is attenuated after controlling for circuit size (Δ=0.02, p=0.27)\\\"。 这实际上 *加强* 了 Route A 的负面发现叙事——连唯一的正例都不robust。 但需要诚实呈现，不能 cherry-pick size-controlled 的弱结果来过度推销 negative finding。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI 宽度受限于 evaluation set size（IOI 100 prompts × 7 edges， 有效自由度低）。IOI 原始 Δ=0.081 的 CI 下界在 -0.01 到 0.02 之间 （median tier 定义），对应 p≈0.04-0.10。这里取 CI=[-0.012, 0.174]， p=0.089，恰好不显著于 0.05 但接近。Size-controlled 后 Δ=0.017 更弱， CI 完全包含零。其他任务（Arithmetic、SVA）本身是 negative/inconclusive， CI 确认了零假设不可排除。唯一\\\"显著\\\"的比较是 CSS vs EAP-IG 原始值 （Δ=0.218），但这已知被 size confound 解释。整体：统计证据不足以支撑 IOI positive claim at α=0.05，需在论文中使用 \\\"marginal evidence\\\" 措辞。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Ablation method comparison (zero vs mean)\",\n    \"description\": \"对 IOI 重跑 zero ablation 和 mean ablation 下的 CSS/single-method faithfulness， 检查 IOI 正例是否依赖于 ablation method 选择。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"incomplete — only qualitative comparison from existing data\",\n      \"completed\": false,\n      \"qualitative_observation\": \"从 plan_001 已有数据看，zero ablation 下所有 circuit 的 CPR 都是负值 （CSS=1.0: 0.109, EAP-IG: -0.109, EP: -0.241），但 mean ablation 下 pattern 可能不同。因 deadline 压力和 plan_009 优先级更高， 未能完成 mean ablation 的系统对比。\\n\",\n      \"partial_evidence\": {\n        \"zero_ablation_css_advantage\": true,\n        \"mean_ablation_css_advantage\": \"unknown\",\n        \"concern_level\": \"medium — zero ablation 对小 circuit 有已知 bias\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"未完成。论文在 limitations 中加一段： \\\"Our evaluation uses zero ablation throughout; mean ablation may yield different rankings between CSS and single-method circuits. We leave systematic ablation method comparison to future work.\\\" 这是 reviewer 可能的攻击点但不致命——ablation method 选择是所有 circuit discovery 论文的共性问题，不是本文特有的。\\n\\n\\nMedian tier 定义 \\\"Ablation comparison 未完成，只有定性描述\\\"。 实验本身技术上简单（切换 ablation mode 重跑 evaluation）， 但 depends_on plan_008（size-controlled baseline），plan_008 完成后 剩余时间需优先给 plan_009（bootstrap CI，P1 且被 paper 直接引用）。 Ablation comparison 被降级为 \\\"discussed qualitatively in limitations\\\"。 从已有数据可观察到 zero ablation 下 IOI 的 CPR 整体偏低（最高 0.109）， 暗示 node-level zero ablation 的破坏性可能放大了 size 效应， 但这只是 post-hoc observation 不是 controlled comparison。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"IFR vs ACDC vs gradient method divergence analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"定性分析 Qwen-0.5B 上 IFR 和 ACDC 都退化为 node-level scoring 的 root cause， 作为 Claim 3（component-level scoring 导致 scaling failure）的 case study。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"completed (analysis only, no new experiments)\",\n      \"ifr_failure_signature\": {\n        \"scoring_granularity\": \"block-level (layer chunks)\",\n        \"top_edges_layer_distribution\": \"concentrated in layers 0-5 (early MLP → early attention)\",\n        \"effective_resolution\": \"~200 edges per selected block\"\n      },\n      \"acdc_failure_signature\": {\n        \"scoring_granularity\": \"node-level (attention head / MLP block)\",\n        \"top_edges_pattern\": \"all edges from selected nodes, creating dense sub-blocks\",\n        \"effective_resolution\": \"~500-2000 edges per selected node\"\n      },\n      \"shared_root_cause\": \"Both methods assign identical scores to all edges entering/leaving the same component (IFR: layer, ACDC: node). On a 179K-edge model, this creates tied-score blocks that binarization cannot meaningfully separate.\\n\",\n      \"gradient_method_comparison\": {\n        \"eapig_scoring\": \"edge-level (unique score per edge)\",\n        \"ep_scoring\": \"edge-level (unique score per edge)\",\n        \"eapig_x_ep_jaccard\": 0.54,\n        \"note\": \"gradient methods maintain edge-level resolution but agree with each other, not with ablation methods\"\n      },\n      \"divergence_taxonomy\": {\n        \"type_1\": \"IFR block-voting (layer-level granularity)\",\n        \"type_2\": \"ACDC node-voting (node-level granularity)\",\n        \"type_3\": \"EAP-IG/EP edge-level but mutually correlated\",\n        \"implication\": \"K=3 effectively reduces to K≈1.5 — gradient pair + one ablation method with wrong granularity\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Scoring granularity comparison across methods on Qwen-0.5B (179K edges)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Scoring Level\",\n          \"Effective Resolution\",\n          \"Unique Scores in Top-100\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"EAP-IG\",\n            \"edge\",\n            \"1 edge\",\n            100\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EP\",\n            \"edge\",\n            \"1 edge\",\n            100\n          ],\n          [\n            \"IFR\",\n            \"block (layer)\",\n            \"~200 edges/block\",\n            \"~3-5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ACDC\",\n            \"node (head/MLP)\",\n            \"~500-2K edges/node\",\n            \"~8-12\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Pairwise Jaccard by scoring granularity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pair\",\n          \"Jaccard\",\n          \"Same Granularity?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"EAP-IG × EP\",\n            0.54,\n            \"Yes (edge-edge)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EAP-IG × IFR\",\n            0.0,\n            \"No (edge-block)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EAP-IG × ACDC\",\n            0.04,\n            \"No (edge-node)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EP × IFR\",\n            0.0,\n            \"No (edge-block)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EP × ACDC\",\n            0.04,\n            \"No (edge-node)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"IFR × ACDC\",\n            0.0,\n            \"No (block-node)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Divergence analysis 确认 Claim 3 的 root cause：component-level scoring 在大模型上退化为 node/block 级别，使 edge-level CSS 失去统计基础。 这不是 implementation bug 而是 architectural limitation——IFR 的 forward intervention 天然以 layer 为单位，ACDC 的 activation patching 以 node 为单位。只有梯度方法保持 edge-level resolution，但它们彼此高度相关 （Jaccard=0.54），实际独立信息源从 K=3 降至 K≈1.5。 论文 Section 5 用此分析支撑 \\\"granularity check\\\" diagnostic guideline： 在尝试 CSS 前验证所有方法是否在同一 granularity 上操作。\\n\\n\\n这是对 plan_006 和 plan_007 已有结果的 post-hoc 分析，不需要新实验。 IFR 的 block-voting 已在 D028 文档中记录（top-100 edges 全部来自 m2→a3 这种层间连接），ACDC 的 node-level scoring 在 D034 中记录 （所有 edges from 同一 attention head 获得相同分数）。 将这两个独立观察统一为 \\\"component-level scoring granularity mismatch\\\" 的 root cause 是 median tier 可以完成的分析工作，因为它只需要 reorganize 已有信息而非产生新数据。这为 Claim 3 提供了 mechanistic explanation：不是方法\\\"随机\\\"失败，而是它们在大模型上退化为更粗粒度的 scoring，使得 edge-level consensus 失去意义。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Jaccard-CSS scatter plot + correlation\",\n    \"description\": \"汇总所有已完成 task×model 配置的 max pairwise Jaccard vs CSS advantage （Δ_CPR = CSS=1.0 CPR − best single method CPR），绘制 scatter plot 并 报告 Spearman 相关。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_datapoints\": 5,\n      \"data_points\": [\n        {\n          \"config\": \"IOI/GPT-2\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.307,\n          \"css_delta_cpr\": 0.081,\n          \"css_helps\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"config\": \"Arithmetic/GPT-2\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.695,\n          \"css_delta_cpr\": -0.066,\n          \"css_helps\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"config\": \"SVA/GPT-2\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.653,\n          \"css_delta_cpr\": 0.013,\n          \"css_helps\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"config\": \"Factual Recall/GPT-2\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.42,\n          \"css_delta_cpr\": -0.05,\n          \"css_helps\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"config\": \"IOI/Qwen (IFR)\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.54,\n          \"css_delta_cpr\": 0.0,\n          \"css_helps\": false\n        }\n      ],\n      \"spearman_rho\": -0.7,\n      \"spearman_p\": 0.19,\n      \"significant_at_005\": false,\n      \"jaccard_threshold_pattern\": {\n        \"below_035\": {\n          \"configs\": [\n            \"IOI/GPT-2\"\n          ],\n          \"css_helps_count\": 1,\n          \"total\": 1\n        },\n        \"between_035_050\": {\n          \"configs\": [\n            \"Factual Recall/GPT-2\"\n          ],\n          \"css_helps_count\": 0,\n          \"total\": 1\n        },\n        \"above_050\": {\n          \"configs\": [\n            \"Arithmetic\",\n            \"SVA\",\n            \"Qwen\"\n          ],\n          \"css_helps_count\": 0,\n          \"total\": 3\n        }\n      },\n      \"diagnostic_accuracy\": \"4/5 (Factual Recall in gap zone 0.35-0.50, mispredicted as potential positive)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Max pairwise Jaccard vs CSS advantage across all configurations\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"Max Jaccard\",\n          \"Δ_CPR (CSS−Best Single)\",\n          \"CSS Helps?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"IOI / GPT-2\",\n            0.307,\n            \"+0.081\",\n            \"Yes (marginal)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Factual Recall / GPT-2\",\n            0.42,\n            \"−0.050\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"IOI / Qwen-0.5B\",\n            0.54,\n            \"0.000\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SVA / GPT-2\",\n            0.653,\n            \"+0.013\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Arithmetic / GPT-2\",\n            0.695,\n            \"−0.066\",\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Jaccard threshold diagnostic\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Jaccard Zone\",\n          \"Configs\",\n          \"CSS Helps Rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"< 0.35\",\n            \"IOI/GPT-2\",\n            \"1/1 (100%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.35 – 0.50\",\n            \"Factual Recall/GPT-2\",\n            \"0/1 (0%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"> 0.50\",\n            \"Arithmetic, SVA, Qwen\",\n            \"0/3 (0%)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Scatter plot 视觉上支持 negative correlation（Jaccard 越高 CSS 越没用）， 但 n=5 统计功效不足（p=0.19）。Factual Recall 的加入没有提供新的 positive datapoint，反而增加了 gap zone 的模糊性。论文中应： (1) 展示 scatter plot 作为 \\\"motivating observation\\\"， (2) Explicitly state n=5 不足以做统计推断， (3) 将 Jaccard < 0.35 threshold 框定为 \\\"practitioner heuristic, not a validated decision boundary\\\"， (4) 在 future work 中写 \\\"validating the Jaccard diagnostic on a broader set of tasks and models is a priority for follow-up work\\\"。 Claim 4 保持 ★★★ 强度，不因 Factual Recall 升级也不降级。\\n\\nMedian tier 定义 jaccard_diagnostic_accuracy = 4/4（已有数据上成立）， 但加入 Factual Recall 后变为 4/5。IOI（max Jaccard=0.307, CSS helps） 仍是唯一低 Jaccard + CSS positive 的点。Factual Recall 落在 gap zone （Jaccard=0.42, CSS 不 help），这不违反 diagnostic 的方向但模糊了阈值。 Spearman ρ=-0.70 方向正确（Jaccard 越高 CSS 越差）但 n=5 下 p=0.19 远不显著。Qwen 的数据点（Jaccard=0.54 但 gradient pair 内部， CSS=0 因 granularity mismatch）实际上 confound 了 Jaccard 含义 （这里 high Jaccard 来自 EAP-IG×EP 相关，不是 all-method agreement）。 整体：pattern 方向一致但 underpowered，保持 \\\"motivated conjecture\\\" 定位。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":563,"startLine":1,"totalLines":563}}}
