{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KJ674JeSnPB4Ck7y1ctACF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the directory exists. Now I need to write a complete LaTeX paper based on the experiment data and paper framing. Let me carefully construct this paper.\n\nThe paper is about \"Cross-method binary consensus in circuit discovery\" - specifically studying when consensus-based circuit selection (CSS) works and when it fails. The key findings:\n\n1. CSS fails on majority of task×model configurations (only IOI on GPT-2 shows marginal advantage)\n2. ACDC isinf binarization creates pathological collapse\n3. Component-level scoring on larger models causes scaling failure\n4. Jaccard as a diagnostic (but underpowered, n=5)\n\n\n5. IOI positive results are marginal and confounded by model size\n\nI need to structure the paper around six main experiments: CSS performance on GPT-2 factual recall, size-controlled baselines for IOI, bootstrap confidence intervals for circuit performance, method comparison ablations, divergence analysis across different circuit discovery approaches, and a correlation study between Jaccard similarity and CSS effectiveness. The target venue is EMNLP 2026 Findings.\n\nNow I'm drafting the LaTeX structure for the full paper.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1917,"cache_read_input_tokens":32343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1917},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad6d974b-308b-4e8c-8a13-29159c8aeb91","uuid":"99860dcc-221b-4ab9-87d4-13ce4a89f01b"}
